  "fixture_ids": [
    "SR-FIX-REQIF-PRESERVATION-v1",
    "SR-FIX-REQIF-LOSS-v1"
  ],
  "preconditions": [
    "Caller-owned source and actual target bytes, explicit source context/hashes and existing ReqIFLimits. No project owner, mapping success or write authority inferred."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Merge complete source bytes into the closed namespaced carrier; verify byte-exact recovery from actual native JSON target bytes, preserved foreign extensions, deterministic source ordering and idempotent merge.",
    "Reject incompatible existing carriers, duplicate keys, tampered size/hash/Base64, noncanonical encodings, changed source/extensions/target bindings and invalid locations without overwriting inputs.",
    "Reuse the structure XML safety reader for every carrier entry; reject active/external content, DTD/entities and budget failures before successful return. Propagate injected host failures.",
    "Inventory actual codec-reported extras and independent attributes; compare actual target content before assigning preservation references. Stable item/loss IDs bind direction, context, source bytes, location and reason. No target bytes or a different context/source cannot prove retention.",
    "Distinguish original-byte roundtrip and explicit partial assessment from native projection, attachment transport, whole-plan success or write authority.",
    "Inventory the entire actually bound XML source including independent metadata, source fields, opaque subtrees, hierarchy/relation data and XHTML originals; derive nonrepresentability from the existing projection, and compare mapped record fields with actual JSON target pointers.",
    "Assess one entire native JSON record candidate against the existing projection of its actual ReqIF target. Inventory remaining native fields, extension entries and relations; an old source capsule does not prove retention of current native edits.",
    "Require safe caller-owned source attachment bytes, validate all XML target references and compare actual supplied file payloads. XML retention alone never certifies attachment transport.",
    "Recompute the bound assessment at the pure export return boundary: reject losses under fail-on-loss and reject missing assessment prerequisites, with an owned machine report and no returned export bytes. Explicitly permitted, completely reported losses remain losses.",
    "Exercise source/target/mapping conflicts, all seven XML budgets, strict JSON syntax, opaque/original attachment safety, typed carrier limits and host exceptions without reclassifying them as ordinary loss."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "ReqIF-Inhalte außerhalb des unterstützten Abbildungsprofils MÜSSEN entweder verlustfrei unter namespaced `extensions` erhalten oder als einzeln identifizierter Informationsverlust im Import- beziehungsweise Exportplan ausgewiesen werden.",
    "scope": "14.j.W passive original-source carrier and verified original-byte recovery plus source-derived inventory of codec-reported uninterpreted XML. Actual JSON/XML targets determine preserved versus lost, with deterministic bound item identities. Full assessment, loss_free and native_projection_complete remain false because native mapping/projection and attachment transport are outside this W assessment. General native extensions stay passive. Existing import gates and artifact metadata are unchanged. 14.j.R adds complete bound-input inventories for original-source transport, whole XML mapped-record assessment with all remainders, and one entire native JSON record candidate compared with actual XML. Native projection, assessment completeness and loss freedom are separate. Every source information unit without a proved mapping is retained only by the two actual-target v1 forms or explicitly lost. Actual attachment payloads are checked separately. The pure export boundary returns no bytes on blocked loss/incomplete assessment; it performs no writes. Existing W partial reports and import authorization gates retain their contracts."
  },
